7839],[-99.60398,44.88354],[-99.59754,44.88601],[-99.59644,44.88617],[-99.59595,44.88568],[-99.59641,44.88516],[-99.61484,44.87739],[-99.61576,44.87757],[-99.61565,44.87839]]},{"t":7,"ef":"EF1","ring":[[-99.61539,44.87787],[-99.61462,44.87849],[-99.61178,44.87981],[-99.61061,44.88009],[-99.61081,44.87963],[-99.61408,44.87798],[-99.61539,44.87787]]},{"t":5,"ef":"EF0","ring":[[-99.16005,45.49988],[-99.16014,45.50007],[-99.15643,45.5033],[-99.15424,45.505],[-99.15003,45.50765],[-99.14555,45.51003],[-99.15228,45.50614],[-99.15406,45.50488],[-99.15986,45.49993],[-99.16005,45.49988]],"kind":"swath"}],"dpts":[[45.44909,-99.74676,"EF2",0,"4 Miles W of Bowdle: Small Barns or Farm Outbuildings (SBO)","Total Destruction of building \u2014 appears to be initial touchdown point for tornado. trees are broken off in a westerly direction on west side of property, while debris on east side of property is thrown northeast. roof/gutter/shingle damage to main house but in",2],[45.47417,-99.7011,"EF1",0,"2.5 Miles NW of Bowdle: Trees: Hardwood (TH)","Trees uprooted \u2014 large trees tipped over. machine shed doors blown off. roof damage to main residence. grain bins destroyed and not certain of where they are. tractor trailer pivoted 90 degrees and moved 10 feet. old grain trailer lifted and moved 100 yds to t",2],[45.47292,-99.66749,"EF3",0,"1.5 Miles N of Bowdle: Small Barns or Farm Outbuildings (SBO)","Collapse of walls \u2014 unoccupied residence left untouched. few outbuildings damaged. worse damage to outbuilding near 325th ave. on backside of house 4 gravity bin carts were blown/rolled about 100 yds from initial parking spot. trees in back of house also blown",2],[45.47744,-99.65544,"EF4",0,"1.5 miles N of Bowdle: Trees: Hardwood (TH)","Trees debarked with only stubs of largest branches remaining \u2014 most property damage. loss of 2 garages with one vehicle lifted 100 yds through the trees before coming to rest. major property damage with trees completely debarked",2],[45.6053,-98.93186,"EF1",0,"HWY45 Near Wetonka: Metal Building System (MBS)","Metal roof or wall panels pulled from building \u2014 metal buildings (calfing barn) down, sheet metal thrown approx 300 yards\ngrain bin knocked over \nhorses injured, cows and calves injured and missing\nchimney on house knocked over \npics through 824",6],[45.60554,-98.82845,"EF1",0,"Long Lake Colony: Metal Building System (MBS)","Metal roof or wall panels pulled from building \u2014 long lake colony turkey barns with roof and wall damage, sheet metal dispursed and wrapped around poles\n\npic 835-833",6],[45.62088,-98.7671,"EF1",0,"Wetonka: Trees: Softwood (TS)","Trees uprooted \u2014 trees near neon moon bar",6],[45.86376,-98.30589,"EF2",0,"West of Helca:  "," ",9]],"sources":[{"title":"NWS Aberdeen \u2014 May 22, 2010 South Dakota tornado tracks","url":"https://noaa.hub.arcgis.com/maps/noaa::may-22nd-south-dakota-tornado-tracks-including-the-bowdle-sd-ef4-tornado","used":"EF contours for every track, survey points"},{"title":"NOAA Storm Events Database","url":"https://www.ncdc.noaa.gov/stormevents/","used":"county-by-county positions, clock times, widths, ratings and survey narratives"}],"episodes":[{"wfo":"ABR","text":"Several supercell thunderstorms developed along a very strong warm front and produced nine tornadoes from Akaska to Bowdle to Hecla. The largest of the tornadoes was an EF4 tornado which occurred near Bowdle. This tornado produced devastating damage in the Bowdle area. The other tornadoes ranged from EF0 to EF2 and caused extensive tree and building damage. Nearly one-hundred power poles were downed along with several high line towers leaving nearly a thousand customers without power. Also, very strong straight line winds and large hail up to the size of golfballs affected parts of the area causing some damage."},{"wfo":"LBF","text":"Thunderstorms developed along a semi-stationary front that stretched north to south across the Central Plains. By late evening, the front extended south near Highway 83 in northeast Cherry County. The storms rapidly intensified moving northeastward and produced large hail up to 1.25 inches and two tornadoes."},{"wfo":"UNR","text":"Large hail and strong wind gusts accompanied a severe thunderstorm over southern Todd and Tripp Counties. A tornado crossed the town of Winner, causing minor damage in town and destroying two barns east of town."}],"story":["On 22 May 2010 a slow-moving supercell over north-central South Dakota put down a series of tornadoes over open prairie, in clear air, in front of a small army of storm chasers.","The strongest, near Bowdle, grew into a wide, textbook wedge and was filmed from close range for almost its whole life. It was rated EF4 on the damage it did to the few farmsteads in its way, and nobody was hurt.","The day is one of the best-documented tornado events on record for exactly that reason: hours of footage from every side, of a storm that stayed away from people."],"facts":[{"label":"Rating","value":"EF4"},{"label":"Casualties","value":"None"},{"label":"Filmed","value":"Almost its whole life","note":"From close range, in clear air"}]}